# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_account_scope_erase_enumeration.py" "ACCOUNT-SCOPE ERASE/PURGE ENUMERATION GATE: PASS" "account-scope erase enumeration" "account-scope erase/purge enumeration (audit iter-5 P1: a STRUCTURAL invariant tying the per-account table set to the two lifecycle-forget fns so the NEXT new table cannot silently reopen the GDPR-erase / uninstall-purge gap [it already fired once for webhook_delivery]. Introspects pg_attribute for EVERY core.* table carrying account_id/account_key/grantor_account/followed_account and asserts via pg_get_functiondef: ERASE [the GDPR hard delete] references EVERY such table [full completeness -- any miss is a FAIL], and PURGE [the uninstall WORKING-SET forget] references every such table EXCEPT a documented RETAIN allowlist [identity/append-only-ledger/routing/delegation+social/policy/store_connection are deliberately retained on uninstall -- an uninstall is not a hard delete]; plus allowlist hygiene [no typo'd or dead retain entry]. A new per-account table lands red until consciously handled in BOTH paths)" "account-scope erase/purge enumeration / lifecycle-forget completeness (catalog-introspecting structural gate: erase covers ALL account-scoped tables, purge covers the working-set subset modulo a documented retain allowlist; the next new table can't silently reopen the privacy gap; SECURITY/PRIVACY-critical)" 30
